Aaron Sampson here emerging from two  weeks of playing destiny and raising a  newborn baby even though I had my hands  full of blue purple and greenish brown  n-grams yeah I still manage to do some  non destiny related shooting of which  I'm about to tell you the first thing  happened in battlefield 4 now in its  terminal stage I mean final stand stage  which came out with four playable maps  in their community test environment I'm  happy to say that map design in  battlefield 4 keeps getting better and  better if naval strike was the aquatic  dlc final stand would be the  subterranean dlc almost every map having  it built out bunker complex that leads  to intense infantry combat and also adds  tactical death you control the interior  of the map on foot or do you control the  exterior with vehicles to really cool  map features that stood out were first  off on hangar 21 a massive hangar where  a titan is under construction not to  mention this big-ass engine testing  exhaust port underneath and the other  particularly cool feature was on the  giants of Corellia map and involved a  giant collapsible ceiling that makes up  for one not being an operation Locker  and in case you missed it this thematic  dlc is a prequel to battlefield 2142  future weapons also abound in final  stand you've got a hover tank which at  this stage seems to be kind of like a  just hard to control tank you've got the  xt-1 minigun UAV which reigns death from  the sky you have the SC 42 which is a  bullet spewing monster that also  hilariously juggles vehicles in the  alpha and you've got pod launchers on  hangar 21 that allow players to leapfrog  up and down the mountainside I think I'm  forgetting something oh yeah the railgun  Q silly music  I need to work on that one a bit my  overall early impressions of final stand  is that it looks like enough new content  for players to return to battlefield 4  for one last hurrah I respect dice for  going back to thematic DLC in future  weapons because at least did something  different with battlefield 4 wrapping up  all I have to say is the next  battlefield had better launch on a  stable platform get rid of the painful  scoop unlock grinding system ditch that  god-awful Battle Pack fiasco and stop  reusing assets for me to even consider  it moving on to the other game I played  last week  the other thing that you may have missed  in the destiny hype week is titanfall  dropped its last DLC titled IMC rising  I've made no secret of my love for this  game it's rare that a developer says  something like 6v6 no trust us and  people react skeptically then they prove  everyone wrong more than any other  shooter in recent memory titanfall  nailed basic shooting and movement  mechanics while making conscious  decisions like everyone gets a Titan the  ability to eject the smart pistol and  grunts to make sure anyone at any skill  level can have fun IMC rising continues  in the tradition of stellar map design  exciting Titan fights and fantastic park  or rather than talk a lot about this  last DLC I'd rather leave on a few  thoughts for titanfall sequel the next  titanfall should push the multiplayer  campaign much further and not be afraid  to get players involved directly in plot  points this means that unlike in the  first titanfall the game can't be afraid  of having campaign winners and campaign  losers also the campaign shouldn't be  afraid to include a PVE aspect shoot a  dragon you should draw aggro shoot a  big-ass brontosaurus and maybe even  encourage both teams to pause fighting  to handle a greater threat the next  titanfall should also distinguish the  two sides better militia needs to have  more beat up more jury-rigged titans in  gear also the black market system  implemented in frontiers edge should  lead to extremely unique weapons and  equipment which it doesn't go nearly far  enough on at present finally titanfall  hints at so much lower between matches  it's clear that it exists respawn should  cough it up alright well back to destiny  until Borderlands pre-sequel launches  next month be sure to check out the  hilarious playing is for claptraps in  borderland the pre-sequel video on  gamespot extra points if you find the  flappy birds reference Aaron out  you
 

